    thinking: "**Developing TurnosGrid Component**\n\nI\'ve successfully established the `PlanesPricing.tsx` file. My next objective is to design `/src/components/TurnosGrid.tsx`, which will focus on Module 3. This component\'s layout will include a weekly grid format with times as rows, days as columns, and cells displaying `X/cupo`. I\'m starting to think about applying specific colors: green for less than 70% capacity, and yellow for 70-90%.\n\n\n**Refining TurnosGrid Details**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the `/src/components/TurnosGrid.tsx` design. I\'ve decided on color coding: red for >= 90% capacity, and green for less than 70%, with yellow for the intermediate range. Cell clicks will reveal a list of assigned clients, distinguishing between fixed and flexible appointments. I\'m also planning automatic waitlisting for full slots. The grid itself will feature tabbed links for weekly viewing and recovery management, including a uniform matrix design.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `/src/components/TurnosGrid.tsx` to build the weekly schedule planner. It sets up columns for weekdays (Mondays through Fridays) and rows representing specific hour slots. The cells show real-time ratios of `Occupied / Capacity` with colors indicating saturation levels (green for under 70%, yellow for 70%-90%, and red for 90% or higher). Selecting a cell displays a panel showing fijos and flexible members, waiting list lines, and allows changing maximum slot capacities without affecting current schedules. It also hosts the recovery workspace to schedule missed classes."
