    thinking: "**Considering Layout Options**\n\nOkay, I\'m now exploring the optimal layout design. I\'m focusing on \"Geometric Balance\" and considering a grid or flexbox arrangement. Specifically, I\'m thinking about a sidebar, left pane on desktop, with a slate-900 background. I\'m contemplating how to replace `App.tsx` completely, but I will continue my examination of the layout first.\n\n\n**Refining Style and Structure**\n\nI\'m now focusing on stylistic elements, aiming for a consistent aesthetic. My color scheme leans toward a slate palette with highlights and decorations in sky-400. I envision an Argentina date header with a ticking time element. Also, I am carefully constructing the new `App.tsx` layout and have confirmed that a single, contiguous block edit can replace its entire content, using a single `edit_file` call.\n\n\n**Drafting Component Import**\n\nI\'m now drafting the component import section. I\'ve successfully imported `useState` and `useEffect` and all relevant context and visual components. The type definition for `TabID` is also ready for implementation. This section looks quite good to go, I think.\n\n\n**Implementing Core App Structure**\n\nI\'m now implementing the core application structure within `App.tsx`, wrapping the application with `GymProvider` and rendering `InnerApp`. I\'ve set up the state variables for `activeTab`, `showAddPagoModal`, and `isSidebarOpen`. I\'ve also incorporated `useGym` to access the `rolActivo` context. My attention has turned to incorporating the date and time strings, using `useEffect` for updates, and using `toLocaleTimeString` and `toLocaleDateString` for formatting, though I need to consider formatting options.\n\n\n**Refining Time Display Logic**\n\nI\'m now refining the logic for displaying date and time. I\'ve focused on `toLocaleTimeString` and `toLocaleDateString` for formatting, but I\'m now implementing logic to handle the time zone specifically for Buenos Aires. I\'m also ensuring a robust try-catch block for time formatting and error handling. I\'m incorporating a `setInterval` function to update the time every second.\n\n\n**Defining Tab Content**\n\nI\'m now defining the tab content array, encompassing identifiers, labels, icons, and descriptions for each tab. I\'m leveraging `CalendarRange`, `Landmark`, `ShieldAlert`, `LineChart`, and `ShieldCheck` for tab icons. I\'ve also incorporated a `currentTab` variable for easy reference. I have successfully set up the switch statement for rendering based on the active tab and ensured it defaults to the first tab item if no match is found. My focus now is on implementing the corresponding components, such as `TurnosGrid`, `PagosLog`, and `ClientesCRUD`, based on the current tab.\n\n\n**Implementing Tab Content Rendering**\n\nI\'m now implementing the components within the tab content, specifically focusing on `TurnosGrid`, `PagosLog`, `ClientesCRUD`, `MorososControl`, `ProyeccionesTab`, `AuditLogView`, and `Dashboard`. I\'m integrating the `PagoModal` component, which uses `setShowAddPagoModal`. My focus is on the conditional rendering of these components based on the active tab and the default case.\n\n\n**Constructing UI Header**\n\nI\'m now implementing the UI header, integrating an administration title with a sky-400 color and bold font. I\'ve also incorporated a button for toggling the sidebar visibility, using a Menu icon when closed and an X icon when open. I am ensuring that the toggle button utilizes a transition effect with appropriate hover states, while maintaining the geometric slate-900 background of the main layout, with appropriate padding.\n\n\n**Integrating Sidebar Display**\n\nI\'m now integrating the sidebar display, incorporating the \"ARES GYM\" title and administration subtitle, ensuring alignment with the sky-400 color and bold font style. I\'ve also implemented the navigation list with dynamic tab items, mapping their IDs to activate tab selection, while also closing the sidebar upon selection. I\'m focusing on incorporating the sidebar toggle functionality as well.\n\n\n**Refining Sidebar Navigation**\n\nI\'m now refining the sidebar navigation to be more user-friendly and aesthetically pleasing. I\'m focusing on the visual cues for selected and unselected tab items, as well as incorporating appropriate hover states. The goal is to provide a clear indication of the active tab while maintaining a clean, modern design. I have implemented a conditional styling system, using a ternary expression to select classes based on `isSelected`.\n\n\n**Implementing User Roles**\n\nI\'m now incorporating user role-based display elements in the sidebar. I\'ve added code to display different text for admin vs. operator roles, including specific role titles and an active session indicator. I am also implementing a backdrop for mobile drawer and ensuring it can close the sidebar on a click. This should improve user experience.\n\n\n**Integrating Role Switcher**\n\nI\'m now integrating a role switcher component for enhanced role management. I am also implementing a geometric sub-header with the selected tab\'s description. The current tab\'s description is also in the header, now. I\'ve focused on displaying the subheader\'s tab and date, with a map pin for the location. I\'m focusing on ensuring these elements are consistent with the geometric theme.\n\n\n**Finalizing Date and Time**\n\nI\'m now finalizing the date and time display, ensuring it\'s robust and timezone-aware. Specifically, I have integrated the Argentina location. I\'m leveraging the header, and then integrating the time string, and the date with Argentina localization. The plan is to complete the header, by integrating the components, with a focus on formatting and display accuracy.\n\n\n"
