    modified_response: "I have successfully applied the **Geometric Balance** design theme to Ares Gym. The changes establish a distinctive, high-end, and functional dashboard structure with meticulous typography and responsive grids.\n\n### \360\237\216\250 Visual & Functional Improvements\n\n- **Geometric Grid Layout**:\n  - **Left Navigation Sidebar**: Migrated the horizontal navigation bar into a persistent, premium left sidebar on desktop (`w-[260px]`), styled with a deep Slate-950 (`#050b14` / `#0f172a`) background and crisp, low-contrast Slate borders.\n  - **Responsive Mobile Drawer**: Designed an elegant slide-out navigation drawer with an active indicator badge and standard hamburger toggles to guarantee touch-friendly usage on mobile.\n  - **Active Session Badges**: Added a live user profile card at the base of the sidebar detailing current authorization roles (`Admin Principal` vs `Operativo Guardia`).\n\n- **Interactive Clock & Context Headers**:\n  - Integrated a live ticking real-time clock synced to the `America/Argentina/Buenos_Aires` timezone, paired with a localized date header.\n  - Styled headers using **Inter** and **JetBrains Mono** font-faces for high-contrast, modern visual density.\n\n- **KPI Performance Cards**:\n  - Created a custom hoverable card style (`kpi-card-theme`) with gentle transitions, high-contrast borders (`border-slate-200`), and clean shadow parameters.\n  - Revamped the primary dashboard buttons into a balanced modern slate layout.\n\n- **Console Refinements & Bug Resolution**:\n  - Shifted the top simulation console (`RoleSwitcher`) into a synchronized Sky Blue and Slate-900 style.\n  - Remedied a case-sensitivity bug where clicking the quick shortcut button for the schedule called `setActiveTab(\'turnos\')` instead of the capitalized `\'TURNOS\'` state.\n\nThe application compiles perfectly with zero warnings."
