  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Scheduling Structure**\n\nI\'ve examined `TurnosGrid.tsx` and can confirm that `DIAS` and `HORAS` are indeed the keys determining the scheduling table\'s structure. Now, I\'m shifting focus to `/src/components/SocioPanel.tsx`. It will utilize `useGym` to access and manage key data: `clientes`, `turnos`, `pagos`, `selectedSocioId`, and `asign`.\n\n\n**Refining Time-Based Visualization**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the \"TURNERA DE TIEMPO REAL\" component within the socio panel. The initial grid concept, using DAYS and HOURS, presented some responsive design challenges. I\'ve pivoted towards a more flexible approach: a horizontal \"Selector de D\303\255a\" combined with a list view of time slots. I now have two options: default to a beautiful horizontal segment picker of Days with hour blocks, or to offer both views as options to the user.\n\n\n**Detailing Real-Time Availability**\n\nI\'m deep-diving into the real-time availability display for turn slots. I\'ve figured out how to accurately calculate occupied cupos, considering both fixed and variable assignments, and I\'m planning to display this in a concise badge. The badge will offer insights such as \"Cupos Ocupados: 6/12 (4 fijos + 2 variables)\". Furthermore, I\'ve designed dynamic UI elements based on the client\'s relationship with the slot: highlighting their fixed shift with a specific badge, an \"Liberar Reservado\" button for variable shifts, and a \"Reservar como mi Turno Variable\" for available slots, smartly handling the swap of existing variable shifts with an easy user experience.\n\n\n**Implementing Turn Control**\n\nI\'m now implementing the functionality for users to manage their variable turns. Clients will be able to select from any available slots. If they already have a variable turn, the interface should allow them to release it or pick a new slot. The standard client will receive one variable turn slot. I\'m exploring a simple selector to handle this functionality.\n\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create the `SocioPanel.tsx` file which implements the dedicated client panel containing the quick link to WhatsApp, their full payment history list, and the \"Turnera de Tiempo Real\" for viewing and changing their variable shift."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 407849840
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
