  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering User Access**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how the `RoleSwitcher` interacts with Google login. My current thinking is that, based on a user\'s Google login, we can automatically determine their role within the app. I am taking into account the user\'s requirement for Google sign-in at first access.\n\n\n**Refining Login Flow**\n\nNow, I\'m working to expand the login options. If a user isn\'t logged in, they see a Google Sign-In page to block app access until they log in. After authentication, the email determines the user\'s role. I\'m supporting both `tobiasarraiza17@gmail.com` and `totoarr17@gmail.com` for admin access. Client emails, like `facundo.gomez@gmail.com`, will be matched, setting their role to `SOCIO`. I will include their `selectedSocioId` at that point.\n\n\n**Defining User Access**\n\nI\'ve refined the `SOCIO` access. Now, genuine `SOCIO` users get restricted to the `SocioPanel` with the simulation console hidden. For teachers or operators (`OPERADOR` role), an email like `profe@gimnasio.com.ar` or `profesor@aresgym.com` sets their role accordingly. I\'ll maintain the `RoleSwitcher` only for `ADMIN` or `OPERADOR` to switch roles. For a standard `SOCIO`, the switcher is hidden, but I\'ll add a Google profile widget to display their Google info and a \"Sign Out\" button. I will check `src/GymContext.tsx` to declare Auth fields and view `GymContextType`.\n\n\n**Integrating Google Auth**\n\nI\'m now integrating Google authentication into the `GymContext`. I\'m extending the `GymContextType` interface with `googleUser`, `signInWithGoogle`, and `signOutGoogle` fields. I\'ve successfully reviewed the existing imports in `src/GymContext.tsx`, and I\'m ready to proceed with integrating the authentication functions.\n\n\n**Implementing User Authentication**\n\nI\'m now integrating Google authentication into the context. I\'ll initialize `googleUser` by checking `localStorage` for prior sessions. I\'ll ensure `rolActivo` stays synchronized; I want to default `rolActivo` to the Google user\'s role. If the user changes roles in the simulation, I will update `rolActivo` for admins or operators. I\'ll define how `signInWithGoogle` handles role determination based on email.\n\n\n"
