    thinking: "**Defining User State**\n\nOkay, I\'m defining the `googleUser` state. It looks like loading this from `localStorage` in the `useEffect` on line 82, or in the state initializer is the safest approach. Lazy initialization feels appropriate here, especially in a standard React context.\n\n\n**Refining User Role**\n\nI\'ve refined the approach to initialize `rolActivo`. Now, it defaults to the `role` from `googleUser` if available in `localStorage`. This eliminates a potential race condition and ensures the user\'s role is correctly and immediately loaded on component mount. I\'m leveraging a lazy initialization strategy using the `useState` hook for both `googleUser` and `rolActivo` states.\n\n\n"
