 to `\'ADMIN\'`. I\'m confident about preventing unauthorized privilege escalation. I\'m now fine-tuning the UI in the `RoleSwitcher` to either disable or hide the `\'ADMIN\'` option based on the user\'s Google role. I like the left-side `RoleSwitcher` UI!\n\n\n**Implementing Role Access**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the role access logic within the `/src/components/RoleSwitcher.tsx` component, specifically around lines 30-55. I\'m aiming to disable the \'ADMIN\' role selection button if the `googleUser?.role` is \'OPERADOR\'. This ensures users can\'t escalate their privileges. I\'m carefully reviewing the conditional logic to ensure that an \'OPERADOR\' can\'t select the \'ADMIN\' role. I\'m keen to test this restriction thoroughly to validate security and user access control.\n\n\n"
